      "content": "That makes sense for general uncertainty, but I'm hitting a wall with some specific presentations. We have several cases where the lesions show these strange, almost mottled, greenish-grey discolorations and a coarse, bumpy texture that looks almost... organic in a way that doesn't match typical dermatological models. Specifically, when we see these irregular, crusty patches that seem to spread in a pattern that doesn't follow standard inflammatory routes, how do we differentiate between a localized infection and a more systemic dermatological anomaly in the ICD-10 hierarchy?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
