      "content": "For mottled, greenish-grey discoloration and coarse, crusty patches, you must examine the pattern of involvement and patient history to differentiate etiology. If the presentation strongly suggests a localized infection, use the codes within the infectious disease chapter (e.g., bacterial or fungal infections of the skin). However, if the pattern suggests a wider, non-inflammatory or systemic process, codes for specific dermatoses or neoplasms should be explored, focusing on texture and color as descriptors. Always document the suspected etiology clearly to support the chosen chapter.",
